# Output Structure

abricate_vfdb_results/
    genome1.fna.tsv
    genome2.fna.tsv
    genome3.fna.tsv

Each `.tsv` file contains:
FILE - The filename this hit came from
SEQUENCE - The sequence in the filename
START - 	Start coordinate in the sequence
END - 	End coordinate
STRAND - Strand + or -
GENE - gene name
COVERAGE - What proportion of the gene is in our sequence
COVERAGE_MAP -	A visual represenation of the hit. ==aligned, .=unaligned, /=has_gaps
GAPS - Openings / gaps in subject and query - possible psuedogene?
%COVERAGE -	Proportion of gene covered
%IDENTITY -	Proportion of exact nucleotide matches in the covered part
DATABASE - The database this sequence comes from
ACCESSION - The genomic source of the sequence
PRODUCT - Gene product (if available)


# Notes
- Only the second run of abricate is used in the pipeline.  
